prompt continuation of the same lap -- the rebase brought a red into my own room
think The rebase onto the anointed order brought a peer's docs-geode/lessons/ room -- eight Bhakta lessons and a front door, landed 06:12:33 in commit e40799aba. crushed_index refused: nine unlisted members, eight against docs-geode/wiki/README.md and the room itself against docs-geode/README.md.
think I checked before touching it, because a peer's in-flight work is not mine to index. The commit was 70 minutes old and six commits back on the anointed spine, and upstream's own copies of both indexes carry zero rows for it -- so the red shipped rather than being in flight.
think docs-geode is my shelf, so this is my room's red rather than a claim across a lane. Nine rows: eight on the wiki's shipped-pages table, each naming what its lesson leads to, and one on the shelf front door describing the room and its register.
obs A claim-as-override was unnecessary here and I checked rather than assumed. The distinction that decided it was measurable: whether upstream's OWN indexes carry the rows, which separates a peer mid-lap from a red that has landed.
obs Reading the peer's lessons to write their rows was the cheapest possible review of them, and they read well: Bhakta throughout, show-then-name in lesson 8, and the tree's own teachers credited by name in lesson 6.
obs While indexing press I found its two spelled counts on the shelf front door still read three announcements and one magazine piece against a room of seven; both moved, so the prose and the table agree.
